</style></head><body class="loom-admin-utility loom-backups-page"><div id="loomShellHeader"></div><main class="wrap"><section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">SYSTEM OWNER · PORTABLE RECOVERY</div><h1>Backup & Restore</h1><p>Move the whole LOOM installation, individual projects, or one fully encapsulated person without mixing those scopes together.</p><div class="nav"><a href="../">⚙️ Admin</a></div><div class="tabs"><button class="tab active" data-tab="global">Global LOOM</button><button class="tab" data-tab="projects">Projects</button><button class="tab" data-tab="users">Users</button></div></section>

<div class="tabpane active" data-pane="global"><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Global LOOM export</h2><p class="muted">Entire installation state: global identities/settings, all projects + project data, and portable database application data. Active auth sessions, database credentials, reset/recovery secrets, and server secrets remain excluded.</p><div class="warn">Full-state bundles can contain sensitive account and application history. System Owner access is required.</div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:12px"><button class="btn primary" data-export="full" data-msg="globalExportMsg">Export entire LOOM</button></div><div id="globalExportMsg" class="msg"></div></section><section class="panel" id="globalImportPanel"><h2>Global LOOM import</h2><p class="muted">Upload a full LOOM bundle, verify it first, then explicitly authorize restore.</p><input id="globalBundle" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip"><div class="actions" style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn primary" data-preview="global">Upload + Preview</button></div><div id="globalImportPreview" class="msg"></div><div id="globalImportActions" style="display:none"><div id="globalMappings"></div><div class="field"><label>Default conflict strategy</label><select id="globalStrategy"><option value="merge">Merge safely</option><option value="replace">Replace safely (rollback snapshot first)</option><option value="create-new">Create new only</option><option value="skip">Skip conflicts</option></select></div><div class="field"><label>Full restore confirmation</label><input id="globalConfirm" placeholder="Type RESTORE LOOM"></div><div class="actions"><button class="btn danger" data-apply="global">Apply full restore</button></div></div></section></div></div>

<div class="tabpane" data-pane="projects"><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Project export</h2><p class="muted">Project files are the application. <b>Project + data</b> adds that project's runtime/state slice for every participant, but it does <b>not</b> contain each person's complete LOOM-wide identity. For a clean migration, export the people you care about separately from the Users tab.</p><div class="warn"><b>Think vertical vs. horizontal:</b> Project + data = everything owned by this project, including user/guest-linked project state. Portable User/Guest = everything owned by that person across all projects. Importing project data alone can restore project records that reference a person, but it is not a substitute for restoring that person's complete identity bundle.</div><div class="field"><label>Project</label><select id="project"></select></div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:12px"><button class="btn" data-export="project" data-msg="projectExportMsg">Project files only</button><button class="btn primary" data-export="project-data" data-msg="projectExportMsg">Project + data</button><button class="btn" data-export="projects" data-msg="projectExportMsg">All project files</button><button class="btn" data-export="projects-data" data-msg="projectExportMsg">All projects + data</button></div><div id="projectExportMsg" class="msg"></div></section><section class="panel" id="projectImportPanel"><h2>Project import</h2><p class="muted">LOOM detects whether the bundle contains project files, project data, or both. Existing-project conflicts are previewed before anything is applied.</p><input id="projectBundle" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip"><div class="actions" style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn primary" data-preview="projects">Upload + Preview</button></div><div id="projectImportPreview" class="msg"></div><div id="projectImportActions" style="display:none"><div id="projectMappings"></div><div class="field"><label>Default conflict strategy</label><select id="projectStrategy"><option value="create-new">Create new only</option><option value="merge">Merge safely</option><option value="replace">Replace safely (rollback snapshot first)</option><option value="skip">Skip conflicts</option></select></div><div class="actions"><button class="btn danger" data-apply="projects">Apply project import</button></div></div></section></div></div>

<div class="tabpane" data-pane="users"><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Portable person export</h2><p class="muted">Export a complete person whether they are a permanent account or a standalone Guest. LOOM follows the person across browser identities, Guest Histories/Profiles, avatars, project identities/state, activity/audit history, permissions, moderation, continuity/referrals, media, and attributable database rows.</p><div class="field"><label>Person</label><select id="person"></select></div><div id="personSummary"></div><div class="warn"><b>Permanent users:</b> their account and password hash travel with them, including attached Guest Histories. <b>Standalone Guests:</b> their canonical Guest ID, browser/client lineage, Guest Profile and all attributable state travel with them. A Guest already attached to a permanent user is intentionally not exported separately because it is already inside that user bundle.<br><br><b>Deliberately not transferred:</b> active login sessions, reset/recovery secrets, database/server credentials, and ordinary-import System Owner authority. If the exported person was the System Owner, the bundle is marked so it can be selected from the special <b>Import Previous System Owner</b> option on a truly blank LOOM install.</div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:12px"><button class="btn primary" id="exportPerson">Export selected person</button></div><div id="personExportMsg" class="msg"></div></section><section class="panel" id="userImportPanel"><h2>Portable person import</h2><p class="muted">Imports either a permanent User or standalone Guest. On a clean destination the original stable IDs are restored; repeated imports resolve as safe merges instead of duplicates. Project-linked data remains dormant by project slug until those projects exist.</p><input id="userBundle" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip"><div class="actions" style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn primary" data-preview="users">Upload + Preview</button></div><div id="userImportPreview" class="msg"></div><div id="userImportActions" style="display:none"><div class="field"><label>Import strategy</label><select id="userStrategy"><option value="merge">Merge / restore this person</option><option value="create-new">Create new only</option></select></div><div class="actions"><button class="btn danger" data-apply="users">Restore person</button></div></div></section></div></div>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Generated backups</h2><p class="muted">Generated bundles stay on protected Instance storage until downloaded or cleaned up.</p><div id="backups" class="table"><div class="muted">Loading…</div></div><h3>Pending database payloads</h3><p class="muted">If a global restore reaches a destination before its database is configured, the portable database payload waits here safely.</p><div id="pending" class="table"></div></section></main><div id="loomShellFooter"></div>
<script src="../../engine/deployment-guard.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/loom-time.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/loom-brand.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/identity.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/loom-global-profile.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/loom-toast.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/share-referrals.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script src="../../engine/loom-shell.js?v=0.15.72"></script><script>
const identity=LoomIdentity.get('loom-admin-backups'),$=s=>document.querySelector(s),esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const previewState={global:null,projects:null,users:null};let personRows=[];
async function jsonFetch(url,opts={}){const r=await fetch(url,{cache:'no-store',...opts});const txt=await r.text();let j;try{j=JSON.parse(txt)}catch{throw new Error(`Server returned ${r.status} ${r.statusText} instead of JSON.`)}if(!r.ok||j.ok===false)throw new Error(j.error||`Request failed (${r.status})`);return j}
async function post(body){return jsonFetch('../../api/backup.php',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({clientId:identity.clientId,...body})})}
function showTab(name){document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x.dataset.tab===name));document.querySelectorAll('.tabpane').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x.dataset.pane===name));history.replaceState(null,'',`#${name}`)}document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>showTab(x.dataset.tab));
async function loadProjects(){const j=await jsonFetch(`../../api/projects.php?clientId=${encodeURIComponent(identity.clientId)}&_=${Date.now()}`);const rows=j.projects||[];$('#project').innerHTML=rows.map(p=>`<option value="${esc(p.slug||p.project)}">${esc(p.name||p.slug||p.project)}</option>`).join('')||'<option value="">No projects</option>'}
function renderPersonSummary(){const key=$('#person').value,p=personRows.find(x=>x.key===key);if(!p){$('#personSummary').innerHTML='';return}const guest=p.kind==='guest';const detail=guest?`${Number(p.clientCount||0)} browser identit${Number(p.clientCount||0)===1?'y':'ies'} · ${Number(p.projectCount||0)} project reference${Number(p.projectCount||0)===1?'':'s'}`:`${esc(p.email||'No email')} · account handle ${esc(p.accountHandle||'—')} · ${esc(p.privilege||'User')} · ${Number(p.projectCount||0)} project reference${Number(p.projectCount||0)===1?'':'s'}`;$('#personSummary').innerHTML=`<div class="usercard"><div class="dot">${esc((p.displayName||'?').slice(0,1).toUpperCase())}</div><div><b>${esc(p.displayName)}</b> <span class="pill">${guest?'GUEST':'PERMANENT'}</span>${p.isSystemOwner?' <span class="pill">SYSTEM OWNER</span>':''}<small>${detail}</small>${!p.exportable?`<small class="bad">Already attached to permanent user ${esc(p.coveredByPermanentUser||'')}; export that permanent user instead.</small>`:''}</div></div>`;$('#exportPerson').disabled=!p.exportable}
async function loadUsers(){try{const j=await post({action:'person-list'});const users=(j.users||[]).map(u=>({...u,kind:'user',key:'user:'+u.userId,exportable:true})),guests=(j.guests||[]).map(g=>({...g,kind:'guest',key:'guest:'+g.guestId}));personRows=[...users,...guests];const userOptions=users.map(u=>`<option value="${esc(u.key)}">${esc(u.displayName)}${u.isSystemOwner?' · SYSTEM OWNER':''} · permanent</option>`).join(''),guestOptions=guests.map(g=>`<option value="${esc(g.key)}" ${g.exportable?'':'disabled'}>${esc(g.displayName)}${g.isSystemOwner?' · SYSTEM OWNER':''} · Guest${g.exportable?'':' · included with permanent user'}</option>`).join('');$('#person').innerHTML=`${userOptions?`<optgroup label="Permanent users">${userOptions}</optgroup>`:''}${guestOptions?`<optgroup label="Standalone Guests">${guestOptions}</optgroup>`:''}`||'<option value="">No portable people found</option>';renderPersonSummary()}catch(e){$('#person').innerHTML='<option value="">System Owner required</option>';$('#personSummary').innerHTML=`<div class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</div>`}}$('#person').onchange=renderPersonSummary;
async function loadBackups(){try{const j=await post({action:'list'}),rows=j.backups||[];$('#backups').innerHTML=rows.length?`<table><thead><tr><th>Created</th><th>Type</th><th>Scope</th><th>Size</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(x=>`<tr><td>${esc(window.LoomTime?.format?.(x.createdAt)||new Date(x.createdAt).toLocaleString())}</td><td><span class="pill">${esc(x.type)}</span></td><td><b>${esc(x.scopeLabel||(x.project||'LOOM'))}</b>${x.project?`<br><code>${esc(x.project)}</code>`:''}</td><td>${(Number(x.size||0)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MB</td><td><a class="btn" href="${esc(x.downloadUrl)}">Download</a> <button class="btn danger" data-delete="${esc(x.backupId)}">Delete</button></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`:'<div class="muted">No generated backups yet.</div>';document.querySelectorAll('[data-delete]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=async()=>{if(!confirm('Delete this generated backup?'))return;await post({action:'delete',id:b.dataset.delete});loadBackups()});const pending=j.pendingDatabase||[];$('#pending').innerHTML=pending.length?`<table><thead><tr><th>Created</th><th>Tables</th><th>Size</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>${pending.map(x=>`<tr><td>${esc(window.LoomTime?.format?.(x.createdAt)||new Date(x.createdAt).toLocaleString())}</td><td>${esc(x.tableCount)}</td><td>${(Number(x.size||0)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MB</td><td><button class="btn" data-db="${esc(x.id)}">Apply to configured DB</button></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`:'<div class="muted">No staged database payloads.</div>';document.querySelectorAll('[data-db]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=async()=>{try{const j=await post({action:'apply-pending-db',id:b.dataset.db,strategy:'merge'});LoomToast?.success?.(`Database payload ${j.result.status}.`);loadBackups()}catch(e){LoomToast?.error?.(e.message)}})}catch(e){$('#backups').innerHTML=`<div class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</div>`}}
function exportMessageEl(button){return $('#'+(button.dataset.msg||'projectExportMsg'))}
document.querySelectorAll('[data-export]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=async()=>{const type=b.dataset.export,project=$('#project').value,projectScoped=type==='project'||type==='project-data',msg=exportMessageEl(b);msg.textContent='Building verified bundle…';try{if(type==='full'&&!confirm('Create a full LOOM state backup? It contains sensitive identity/application history, though active sessions and server secrets stay excluded.'))return;const request={action:'create',type};if(projectScoped)request.project=project;const j=await post(request);msg.innerHTML=`<span class="ok">Created ${esc(j.backup.backupId)} · ${esc(j.backup.scopeLabel||'LOOM')} · ${(Number(j.backup.size||0)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MB</span> <a class="btn" href="${esc(j.backup.downloadUrl)}">Download</a>`;loadBackups()}catch(e){msg.innerHTML=`<span class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</span>`}});
$('#exportPerson').onclick=async()=>{const p=personRows.find(x=>x.key===$('#person').value);if(!p||!p.exportable)return LoomToast?.required?.('Choose an exportable person first.');const permanent=p.kind==='user';if(!confirm(`Export ${p.displayName||'this person'} as a complete portable ${permanent?'permanent user':'Guest'} identity bundle?`))return;$('#personExportMsg').textContent='Tracing the complete person identity graph and attributable data…';try{const req={action:'create',type:p.kind};if(permanent)req.userId=p.userId;else req.guestId=p.guestId;const j=await post(req);$('#personExportMsg').innerHTML=`<span class="ok">Created ${esc(j.backup.backupId)} · ${esc(j.backup.scopeLabel)} · ${(Number(j.backup.size||0)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MB${p.isSystemOwner?' · marked as prior System Owner':''}</span> <a class="btn" href="${esc(j.backup.downloadUrl)}">Download</a>`;loadBackups()}catch(e){$('#personExportMsg').innerHTML=`<span class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</span>`}};
async function uploadPreview(kind){const input=$('#'+(kind==='global'?'globalBundle':kind==='projects'?'projectBundle':'userBundle')),out=$('#'+(kind==='global'?'globalImportPreview':kind==='projects'?'projectImportPreview':'userImportPreview')),actions=$('#'+(kind==='global'?'globalImportActions':kind==='projects'?'projectImportActions':'userImportActions'));const f=input.files[0];if(!f)return LoomToast?.required?.('Choose a LOOM bundle first.');const fd=new FormData();fd.append('clientId',identity.clientId);fd.append('bundle',f);out.textContent='Uploading, checksum-verifying, and inspecting bundle…';actions.style.display='none';try{const j=await jsonFetch('../../api/backup.php',{method:'POST',body:fd});const p=j.preview;previewState[kind]=p;const expected=kind==='global'?['full']:kind==='projects'?['project','project-data','projects','projects-data']:['user','guest'];if(!expected.includes(p.exportType))throw new Error(`This is a ${p.exportType} bundle. Open the matching Backup & Restore tab to import it.`);if(kind==='users'){renderPersonPreview(p,out);actions.style.display='block';return}renderProjectLikePreview(kind,p,out);actions.style.display='block'}catch(e){out.innerHTML=`<span class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</span>`}}
document.querySelectorAll('[data-preview]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>uploadPreview(b.dataset.preview));
function renderProjectLikePreview(kind,p,out){const modes=p.availableImportModes||[],modeLabel=modes.includes('both')?'project files + project data':modes.includes('data')&&!modes.includes('project')?'project data only':modes.length?'project files only':'global state';out.innerHTML=`<b>Verified bundle</b><br>Type: ${esc(p.exportType)} · Source LOOM ${esc(p.sourceLoomVersion||'?')}<br>Projects: ${(p.projects||[]).length}<br>Detected project payload: <b>${esc(modeLabel)}</b><br>Database: ${p.database?.included?'portable payload included':'not included'}<br>Checksums: ${p.verification?.checked||0} verified`;const target=kind==='global'?$('#globalMappings'):$('#projectMappings');target.innerHTML=(p.projects||[]).map(x=>{const available=x.availableImportModes||[],recommended=x.recommendedImportMode||available[0]||'project',modeOptions=[['both','Project files + data'],['project','Project files/settings only'],['data','Project data only']].filter(([v])=>available.includes(v)).map(([v,label])=>`<option value="${v}" ${v===recommended?'selected':''}>${label}${v===recommended?' (recommended)':''}</option>`).join(''),detected=[x.hasProjectStructure?'project files':null,x.hasProjectData?'project data':null].filter(Boolean).join(' + ')||'no restorable project payload';return `<div class="option" data-map-source="${esc(x.slug)}"><b>${esc(x.name)}</b><p>Source <code>${esc(x.slug)}</code> · ${esc(detected)}. ${x.exists?'Destination already exists; safe Replace snapshots before mutation.':'No current conflict.'}</p><div class="field"><label>Destination Instance Project slug</label><input data-map-target value="${esc(x.slug)}"></div>${modeOptions?`<div class="field"><label>Import contents</label><select data-map-mode>${modeOptions}</select></div>`:''}<div class="field"><label>Strategy for this project</label><select data-map-strategy><option value="create-new" ${x.exists?'':'selected'}>Create new only</option><option value="merge">Merge into existing</option><option value="replace" ${x.exists?'selected':''}>Replace safely</option><option value="skip">Skip</option></select></div></div>`}).join('')}
function renderPersonPreview(p,out){const person=p.exportType==='guest'?(p.guest||{}):(p.user||{}),guest=p.exportType==='guest',g=person.graphCounts||{},projects=person.projects||[],missing=projects.filter(x=>!x.installed),sourceId=guest?person.sourceGuestId:person.sourceUserId,targetId=guest?person.targetGuestId:person.targetUserId;out.innerHTML=`<b>Verified portable ${guest?'Guest':'permanent user'}</b><div class="usercard"><div class="dot">${esc((person.displayName||'?').slice(0,1).toUpperCase())}</div><div><b>${esc(person.displayName||sourceId)}</b>${person.wasSystemOwner?' <span class="pill">PRIOR SYSTEM OWNER</span>':''}<small>${guest?'Standalone Guest':`${esc(person.email||'No email')} · ${esc(person.privilege||'User')}`} · mode <b>${esc(person.mode||'?')}</b></small></div></div><div class="statgrid"><div class="stat"><strong>${Number(g.clientIds||0)}</strong><span>linked browser identities</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>${Number(g.guestIds||0)}</strong><span>Guest Histories</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>${Number(g.guestProfileIds||0)}</strong><span>Guest Profiles</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>${projects.length}</strong><span>project references</span></div></div><div class="${person.canApply?'ok':'bad'}" style="margin-top:10px"><b>${person.canApply?'Ready to restore':'Conflict requires attention'}</b>${(person.conflicts||[]).length?'<br>'+person.conflicts.map(esc).join('<br>'):''}</div><div class="warn">${person.samePasswordWillWork?'The restored permanent account keeps the same password. ':''}Ordinary import never takes over System Owner authority. ${person.wasSystemOwner?'On a truly blank LOOM install, use the first-run <b>Import Previous System Owner</b> option with this same bundle to restore this person and bind the new installation safely. ':''}${missing.length?`${missing.length} referenced project${missing.length===1?' is':'s are'} not installed; this person’s project data remains preserved by project slug until those projects are restored.`:'All referenced projects currently exist.'}</div><div class="muted" style="margin-top:8px">Source ${guest?'Guest':'User'} ID: <code>${esc(sourceId)}</code>${targetId&&targetId!==sourceId?` → destination <code>${esc(targetId)}</code>`:''}</div>`;$('#userStrategy').value=person.mode==='exact-create'?'create-new':'merge';$('#userStrategy').querySelector('option[value="create-new"]').disabled=person.mode!=='exact-create'}
function collectProjectImport(kind,p){const map={},strategies={},modes={},root=kind==='global'?$('#globalMappings'):$('#projectMappings');root.querySelectorAll('[data-map-source]').forEach(row=>{map[row.dataset.mapSource]=row.querySelector('[data-map-target]').value.trim();strategies[row.dataset.mapSource]=row.querySelector('[data-map-strategy]').value;modes[row.dataset.mapSource]=row.querySelector('[data-map-mode]')?.value||'auto'});return {projectMap:map,projectStrategies:strategies,projectImportModes:modes}}
async function applyImport(kind){const p=previewState[kind];if(!p)return;const out=$('#'+(kind==='global'?'globalImportPreview':kind==='projects'?'projectImportPreview':'userImportPreview'));let body={action:'apply',importId:p.importId};if(kind==='users')body.strategy=$('#userStrategy').value;else{Object.assign(body,collectProjectImport(kind,p));body.strategy=kind==='global'?$('#globalStrategy').value:$('#projectStrategy').value;if(kind==='global')body.confirm=$('#globalConfirm').value}try{const j=await post(body);out.innerHTML=`<span class="ok"><b>Import complete.</b></span><pre>${esc(JSON.stringify(j.result,null,2))}</pre>`;$('#'+(kind==='global'?'globalImportActions':kind==='projects'?'projectImportActions':'userImportActions')).style.display='none';await Promise.all([loadBackups(),loadUsers()])}catch(e){out.innerHTML=`<span class="bad">${esc(e.message)}</span>`}}
document.querySelectorAll('[data-apply]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>applyImport(b.dataset.apply));
(async()=>{try{await LoomShell?.mount?.({apiBase:'../../api',identity,pageTitle:'Backup & Restore',links:[{label:'⚙️ Admin',href:'../'}]});await Promise.all([loadProjects(),loadUsers(),loadBackups()]);const h=location.hash.slice(1);if(['global','projects','users'].includes(h))showTab(h);if(new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('mode')==='import')showTab('projects')}catch(e){document.body.innerHTML=`<div style="padding:30px;font-family:system-ui"><h1>Backup & Restore failed</h1><p>${esc(e.message)}</p><a href="../">Return to Admin</a></div>`}})();
</script></body></html>
